Molecular Assembly here
Traditional semiconductor fabrication relies on high temperatures, vacuums, and toxic chemical etchants that
instantly denature biological proteins. BOPASL-V1 bypasses this via Programmed Molecular Self-Assembly:
Scaffolding (DNA Origami): The structural backbone of each layer is constructed using DNA origami templates and designer peptide scaffolds that pre-program precise spatial coordinates for functional elements.
Biomimetic Deposition: Functional units (crystallins, quantum-dot-doped FRET proteins, and FF-peptide nanotubes) are anchored to the scaffolding in an aqueous, physiological buffer solution at $37^\circ\text{C}$ and pH 7.4.Enzymatic Ligation: Cross-linking and final integration of layers are catalyzed via targeted bio-enzymes (such as tissue
transglutaminase and specific ligases) triggered by localized, non-destructive optical impulses, preserving native protein folding and transparency like that.
Kinematic & Scleral Anchoring
Scleral Haptics (Extended Diameter): The lens is engineered with a 15.0 mm outer diameter,
resting entirely on the insensitive, stable sclera (white of the eye) rather than the highly sensitive and dynamic cornea.
The lower quadrant of the peripheral ring (Layer 5/10) incorporates a higher density of packed melanin and ferritin clusters,
creating a weighted gravitational bias that forces the lens to maintain a rigid vertical orientation.
Epithelial Micro-Locking: The posterior surface features a sub-micron replica of the conjunctival epithelial micro-relief,
generating capillary surface tension and mechanical interlocking to completely eliminate rotational drift.

